<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00A8">Example <span data-tag="00A8">2.3.1.15</span> <span class="named">($2$-Simplices of the Duskin Nerve)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a bicategory. Using Proposition <a data-tag="00A2" href="/tag/00A2">2.3.1.9</a>, we see that a $2$-simplex $\sigma $ of the Duskin nerve $\operatorname{N}^{\operatorname{D}}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ can be identified with the following data: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
A triple of objects $X,Y,Z \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A triple of $1$-morphisms $f: X \rightarrow Y$, $g: Y \rightarrow Z$, and $h: X \rightarrow Z$ in the bicategory $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (corresponding to the faces $d^{2}_2(\sigma )$, $d^{2}_0(\sigma )$, and $d^{2}_1(\sigma )$, respectively). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A $2$-morphism $\mu : g \circ f \Rightarrow h$, which we depict as a diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  Y \ar [dr]^{g} \ar@ {=&gt;}[]+&lt;0pt,-15pt&gt;;+&lt;0pt,-30pt&gt;^-{\mu } &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]_{h} &amp;  &amp;  Z. } \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
